      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-20314",
      ":question/problem": "A boat travels downstream on a river. The table below gives the speed $v(t)$, in miles per hour, of the boat at certain moments during its journey.\n\n| $t\\text{\u00a0(hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v\\text{\u00a0(mi/hour)\u00a0}$ | $32$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\n Use the right Riemann sum for $v(t)$ over $[0,1.5]$ with five subintervals to approximate the total distance traveled by the boat.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*"
